          "create_time": 1793242244.749,
          "update_time": 1793242246.56,
          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "The cosine tilt has a direct classical interpretation: its solution is a Bessel-weighted sum of translates of the original field. After removing an amplitude factor, it is also a symmetric jump-process average for nonnegative auxiliary time. The survey will explain this connection, along with what it does and does not imply for zero motion or computational cost."
            ]
          },
